// The executable's icon, linked into text-editor-vexel-demo.exe (-Pnative-release) and text-editor-vexel-demo-debug.exe (-Pnative).
//
// Ordinal 1, and it is the only icon here, because Windows shows a program's *lowest-numbered* icon resource
// wherever it shows the program itself -- Explorer, the taskbar's pinned button, a shortcut, the Apps entry.
//
// The running window wears the same file: the pom also puts editor.ico on the class path, and @VexelApp's
// icon names it, so the window, its taskbar button and the .exe cannot drift apart. It starts as the framework's
// "new app" mark, and editor.svg is its source. To make it yours, draw an SVG and render it at every size
// Windows asks for (16 to 256 px) into this one .ico; vex-suite-common's tools/Ico.java does exactly that.
1 ICON "editor.ico"

// The manifest: PerMonitorV2 DPI awareness and the OS compatibility java.exe declares, so this executable is
// drawn at the display's real pixels exactly as a JVM launch is, rather than rendered at 96 DPI and stretched by
// Windows. Resource 1 of type 24 (RT_MANIFEST) is the one the loader reads for a process.
1 24 "text-editor-vexel-demo.manifest"
